      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "H3 A40 IDENTITY STUDIO 2026-11-13.a40.1\n\nNative H3 VIDEO model to ONE still PNG. MiniMax H3 and Eros are both available in the same model dropdown.\nINT8 diffusion + INT8 32B reference encoder + FP16 video VAE. No BF16 full stack or four-bit encoder.\nStart: 3.1 seconds, 1.0 MP native video setting, 2.5 MP output, up to two selected face/body photos. The stock conditioning node may resize native video further to its 768-short-edge canvas; exact size is logged.\nThe four native preview thumbnails do NOT mean only four frames are used. Default clip retains 73 frames when source permits.\nSeed-only reruns reuse the separate encoding node through ordinary ComfyUI execution caching. Changing prompt/references/settings can rerun encoding. The cache is not persistent across restart.\nStandard H3: 50 steps, ER-SDE/simple, no Turbo. Eros Fix1: 8 steps, Euler/simple, 12/3 shift, baked Turbo. No extra Turbo adapters, Spectrum, VSA, Sage or approximate denoising caches.\nNo 2 MP native override. Duration UI is 0.25-6 seconds; decoded-pixel guard restored. 4 MP OUTPUT is an optional final test, not a proven A40 memory limit or a guaranteed quality increase.\nPhoto tags follow enabled slot order. Video is <Video 1> in Auto mode. Preview references before rendering. With Keyframes for all engines, use 1-8 extracted frames and watch the nine-image total.\nThe focused image downloads four assets only. Older workflow files and existing models are never deleted.\nMask protection is final compositing, NOT diffusion inpainting. Pose drift inside the mask can still happen.\nSave an edited workflow under your own name. No GPU benchmark or identity-quality test was run by the author.\nPowered by MiniMax H3. Use only with applicable model authorization."
      ]
    }
